// Typecheck this app's SOURCE **and** its `test/` files.
//
// Why a second project rather than adding `test/**/*.ts` to the sibling tsconfig.json: that
// file is the BUILD config (`outDir: "dist"`). Keeping its `include` at `src/**` is what
// mechanically guarantees `dist/` can never gain test files — a stronger guarantee than "we
// remembered to set rootDir". This project is typecheck-only and emits nothing at all.
//
// It runs via this app's `typecheck` script, which the root `pnpm typecheck`
// (`tsc -b && pnpm -r run typecheck`) fans out to and CI gates on. Before #1099 the test files
// were checked by NOTHING: the only project that existed stopped at `src/**`, and vitest
// transpiles specs through swc, which STRIPS types without checking them.
//
// NOTE — deliberately NOT like the packages/* siblings, which relax `module`/
// `moduleResolution`/`lib` to model the ESM runtime vitest actually loads specs in. Those
// packages can afford it because the root tsconfig.json REFERENCES them, so `tsc -b` still
// gates their `src` under the strict node16/es2021 build settings. `apps/*` are not in that
// references list, so this project is the ONLY gate this app's `src` has, and relaxing
// anything here would quietly weaken it. It typechecks clean as-is, so there is nothing to buy.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    // The build config pins rootDir to "src"; test/ sits outside it. Safe to widen precisely
    // because this project emits nothing, so rootDir has no layout consequence.
    "rootDir": ".",
    "types": ["node", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"]
}
